course: dictionary
lesson: 9441
title: Stalagmites and stalactites
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stalagmite is a pointed column of rock that grows up from the floor of a cave. Its name is a clue: stalag-MITE, with the g for ground, so it grows up from the ground. «Stalactites hang from cave roofs and stalagmites grow up from the floor, built from dripping water.»
explain: Water dripping in a cave carries tiny bits of minerals dissolved in it. Each drip leaves a little rock behind. «Drip by drip the water leaves stone behind, growing stalactites that hang down from the roof and stalagmites that grow up from the floor.» Drip by drip, the column gets taller.
explain: Stalactites hang down from the ceiling, and stalagmites grow up from the floor. A stalactite holds tight to the ceiling, so the c in stalactite can stand for ceiling. When a stalactite and a stalagmite meet, they join to make one column. Stalagmites grow extremely slowly, so one can take a very long time to become tall.
fact: A stalagmite is a pointed column of rock that grows up from the floor of a cave.
fact: A stalagmite is made by drips of water full of dissolved minerals.
fact: A stalactite hangs down from the ceiling of a cave; a stalagmite grows up from the floor.
fact: When a stalactite and a stalagmite join, they make a column.
fact: Stalagmites grow extremely slowly, drip by drip.
exercise: «Stalactites hang from cave roofs and stalagmites grow up from the floor.» Which way does a stalagmite grow? | Sideways along the walls | Down from the roof | Out of the water | *Up from the floor
exercise: «Stalagmites grow up from the floor, built from dripping water.» What builds a stalagmite? | Wood and fallen leaves | *Dripping water that leaves rock behind | Ice from the cold | Sand blown in by the wind
exercise: Mia says a stalagmite hangs from the ceiling of a cave. What is wrong with her idea? | It grows in the sea, not in caves | *A stalagmite grows up from the floor, so it does not hang from the ceiling | It is made of wood | It is a stalactite, not a stalagmite, so it hangs down
test: «Drip by drip the water leaves stone behind.» What does drip by drip suggest? | Very fast, like a flood | *Very slowly, one small drop at a time | Only once, at the very start | In the dark only
test: Which pair is correct? A stalactite is the one that | *hangs down from the ceiling | is made of wood | grows up from the floor | is always in the sea
exam: Which way does a stalagmite grow, and where does it start? | Sideways from the wall | Down from the roof | *Up from the floor | Out of the water
